<title>USA: Noise Cancellation says partner signs deal.</title>
<headline>Noise Cancellation says partner signs deal.</headline>
<dateline>STAMFORD, Conn. 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Noise Cancellation Technologies Inc said Thursday a division of a company with which it has a partnership has entered into a licensing agreement with NEC of Japan and Samsung of Korea .</p>
<p>Noise Cancellation said NXT, a division of Verity Group PLC, has an agreement with the two Asian companies to make wafer thin flat panel loudspeakers for the PC, multimedia and domestic audio markets.</p>
<p>The company said NEC anticipates using the new wafer thin loudspeaker technology in up to 100,000 units per month.</p>
<p>The company said it announced a technology cross licensing agreement with Verity on April 1.</p>
</text>
